          "message": {
            "text": "CWE-88 - Unknown vulnerability type\nVulnerability: OS Command Injection via Unvalidated executeCommand Input\nDescription: A critical OS command injection vulnerability exists in the executeCommand() method of the App class.\nThe method accepts arbitrary user-controlled input via the 'data' parameter and passes it directly\nto ProcessBuilder.command() without any validation or sanitization. Despite a code comment stating\nthat only 'ls', 'pwd', and 'echo' commands are allowed, the implementation completely lacks any\nenforcement mechanism to validate the input against this policy. This allows an attacker to execute\narbitrary OS commands with the privileges of the Java process, leading to potential remote code\nexecution, system compromise, data exfiltration, and denial of service attacks.\n"
          },
